# project.done — 2-kobo-style-sleepscreen-banner-prettified

Completed: 2026-09-14 (THE FINAL BLITZ). Commit range ad73373..project.done
on main (v2.1.4 release commit: eb628a6), pushed to
VirInvictus/2-kobo-style-sleepscreen-banner-prettified.

## What shipped (v2.1.4)

- `allowed_hl_styles` now keys KOReader's real `strikeout` drawer name
  (the old `strikethrough` key could never match); verified against the
  device's v2026.07.2 frontend sources (`readerhighlight.lua`).
- Sleeping with no `lastfile` (file manager, or no book opened yet) no
  longer crashes: `DocSettings:open(nil)` is a hard error on device
  (crashes in `getSidecarFilename`), so the patch now skips the sidecar
  and draws the banner without the highlight section.
- The wallpaper-enum finding was arbitrated and CORRECTED: the patch's
  enum (`cover` / `document_cover` / `random_image`) was already right;
  `document_cover` is KOReader's "custom image or cover" and the legacy
  `image_file` value was migrated away upstream in 2024-04. Only README
  wording and the code comment were aligned.
- New: a "Default (from the config file)" reset entry for Message style
  (a style pick is now undoable from the menu).
- New: font pickers list fonts alphabetically by basename.
- A removed menu font pick falls back to the still-valid B_SETT config
  name before the stock alias.
- The random highlight pick is seeded (unseeded LuaJIT repeated its
  sequence across reboots).
- Internal: one Sidecar guard posture in parseFooterText, the UI instance
  kept in a patch local (not on the UIManager singleton), corrected
  comments, the Pill help string recast (no em-dash).
- Docs: the 24-line prose em-dash sweep across README/roadmap/patchnotes/
  CLAUDE/spec plus the shipped help string; spec status line at v2.1.4;
  README compat-shim claim replaced with what actually degrades;
  RESEARCH_STYLES.md bannered as historical; .clinerules reference
  dropped; device reference corrected to KOReader v2026.07.2; roadmap
  audit block fully ticked with dated notes.
- Tests: harness grown 58 -> 70 checks (wrong-screensaver_type
  pass-through, stale-font fallback, strikeout filter matching, reset
  entry, alphabetical sort, no-lastfile guard), green under Lua 5.4 AND
  LuaJIT locally, and enforced by the new CI workflow
  (.github/workflows/harness.yml, first run green).

